# config/supervision.env - supervision knobs for one firstmate home. Copy this
# into a local, gitignored config/supervision.env and edit.
#
# bin/fm-watch.sh, bin/fm-guard.sh, and bin/fm-watcher-beat-alarm.sh all read
# this file before resolving any knob, so every harness and every scheduler
# context resolves the same values for this home. That matters most for launchd
# and cron, which inherit neither a harness setting nor a shell profile: without
# this file the session-independent watcher-beat alert would compare against a
# different staleness threshold than the guard in the same home.
#
# One NAME=value assignment per line. Blank lines and # comments are ignored,
# and a leading `export ` is accepted. The file is parsed, never sourced: a line
# it cannot understand is skipped on its own rather than dropping the valid
# knobs after it, and this file can never execute code.
#
# A real environment variable ALWAYS wins over this file, so a per-invocation
# override is never overwritten. The file supplies only what the environment
# left unset.
#
# Every knob keeps its own default, so set only the ones you want to change.
# docs/configuration.md's "Environment variables" section lists them all.

# How long the watcher liveness beacon may go untouched before supervision
# counts as down. Shared by the guard and the watcher-beat alert, which needs
# two of these windows before it alerts.
FM_GUARD_GRACE=300

# Seconds between watcher poll cycles.
FM_POLL=15

# Heartbeat scan cadence and its backoff cap.
FM_HEARTBEAT=600
FM_HEARTBEAT_MAX=7200
